  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let's define ScoreScoreScore of an array BBB of length MMM as ∑i=1M∑j=iMf(i,j)\\sum_{i=1}^{M} \\sum_{j=i}^{M} f(i,j)∑i=1M​∑j=iM​f(i,j), where f(i,j)=Bif(i,j) = B_if(i,j)=Bi​ ∣|∣ Bi+1B_{i+1}Bi+1​ ∣|∣ …\\dots… ∣|∣ BjB_jBj​ (Here ∣|∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation)\n\nYou are given an array AAA, consisting of NNN **distinct** elements.\n\nFind the sum of ScoreScoreScore over all N!N!N! possible permutations of AAA.\n\nSince the answer can be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the length of the array.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated **distinct** integers A1,A2,…,AnA_1,A_2, \\dots ,A_nA1​,A2​,…,An​ representing the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the sum obtained modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\leq A_i  \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "Sum of NNN does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105 over all testcases"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n2 3\n4\n343 10 7 47",
        "output": "16\n47160",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: Two permutations of AAA are [2,3][2,3][2,3] and [3,2][3,2][3,2].\n\nScoreScoreScore of [2,3]=f(1,1)+f(2,2)+f(1,2)=2+3+2[2, 3] = f(1, 1) + f(2, 2) + f(1, 2) = 2 + 3 + 2[2,3]=f(1,1)+f(2,2)+f(1,2)=2+3+2 ∣|∣ 3=83 = 83=8.\nScoreScoreScore of [3,2]=f(1,1)+f(2,2)+f(1,2)=3+2+3[3, 2] = f(1, 1) + f(2, 2) + f(1, 2) = 3 + 2 + 3[3,2]=f(1,1)+f(2,2)+f(1,2)=3+2+3 ∣|∣ 2=82 = 82=8.\n\nSo, the required sum is 161616."
      }
    ]
  },
